# Epic close — SWAT (permission and the SWAT work)

**Do not run SWAT** (review swarm, epic status close, GitHub Release) until **both:**

1. **SWAT work is the job this turn.** List: [wrap-on-command.mdc](wrap-on-command.mdc).
2. **Permission this conversation** — they typed **SWAT**, **or** this **CMPH** / **“check in and merge”** is the epic’s last in-scope story (that land includes SWAT).

A mid-epic CMPH is not SWAT permission. Do not start the swarm because the epic looks done. **“Check in and merge”** on the last story checks in the story and the epic together. Do not stop after the story land.

## Quality gates (SWAT)

Run [.cursor/rules/handoff-checklist.mdc](handoff-checklist.mdc) → *SWAT / epic close only*:

1. Code review (code-reviewer)
2. Dead code (dead-code-remover, when that skill is available) on the epic’s new surface
3. Tech debt evaluation (tech-debt-evaluator) → update `TECH_DEBT.md` as needed
4. Tests / coverage (merge-ready command from `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` / `TEST_PLAN.md`)
5. Project readiness (optional / N/A)
6. Security review when relevant (security-reviewer)
7. Tier 2 when the epic’s behavior requires it

Do **not** treat epic close as docs-only and skip review, debt, or tests.

## Then status close

Follow [.cursor/skills/pm-governance/SKILL.md](../skills/pm-governance/SKILL.md) → *Epic close*: mark the epic complete in `PM_PLAN`, sync `doc/PROJECT_STATUS.md` and `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` → *Current state*, write the close note, commit and push the **feature branch**. Merge to `main` only with CMPH permission ([no-auto-merge-main.mdc](no-auto-merge-main.mdc)). **After merge to `main`:** if [RELEASE.md](../../RELEASE.md) says this product cuts epic releases, cut a **GitHub Release** for the public version. Do not wait to be asked. Do not upload to a store until the product doc says it is distributable. See [doc/VERSIONING.md](../../doc/VERSIONING.md).

## Do not auto-do on close

- Start the next epic’s implementation unless the user already asked or **Next** already directed it.
- Retire prototypes or other deferred debt unless the user or plan **Next** says so this session.
- Re-open explicitly cut features.
